kiro_waf  --  behaviour specification only; no code imported, no licence exists
================================================================================

  Author:     hoangtuvungcao
  Repository: https://github.com/hoangtuvungcao/kiro_waf
  Licence:    NONE. The clone has no LICENSE or COPYING file at any depth, and its
              README badge reads "License-Proprietary".
  Commit:     f0c399596801916cb3862300901749407f7e5f5a  (2026-05-31)

  Consulted for the observable behaviour of three mechanisms this fork also needs:
  single-use challenge tokens, challenge-loop bypass, and progressive escalation.
  No source, HTML, JavaScript, schema, or component was copied from it, and
  nothing in this repository is a derivative work of it.

  The reason is not stylistic, and it is recorded so a future reader knows the
  boundary was deliberate rather than overlooked: with no licence there is no
  grant, and with no grant there is no permission to copy. An unlicensed source is
  not a weakly-licensed one. The three behaviours above are described in this
  fork's own words and implemented from scratch in `crates/pingap-challenge`.
  `crates/pingap-waf/tests/provenance.rs` fails the build if the string naming this
  project reaches any file under `crates/`, `src/` or `pingap-*/src/`, which makes
  "specification only" enforced rather than intended.

